Cursor AI Rules

Project: Video Clip Tagger

Purpose:
This repository implements an AI-powered video asset organization system.
The system automatically processes raw video clips and converts them into a structured asset library.

Core Pipeline
video
↓
frame extraction
↓
AI vision recognition
↓
tag generation
↓
rename
↓
library index

Architecture Rules
1 Maintain modular architecture.
Do not merge modules with different responsibilities.
Modules must remain separated:
scanner
frame_extractor
model_provider
tagger
renamer
indexer
api

2 AI Model Providers
All AI model providers must implement the same interface:
analyze_image(image_path)
Return format:
{ "scene": "", "action": "", "object": "" }
Providers must remain interchangeable.

3 File System Rules
Incoming videos are placed in:
~/ai-video-factory/clips
Processed videos are stored in:
storage/library
Metadata file:
storage/library/index.json
Do not change this structure.

4 Naming Convention
Videos must be renamed using:
action_id.mp4
Example:
pour_001.mp4
drink_002.mp4

5 Code Modification Rules
Do not change existing pipeline order.
Do not break compatibility with index.json.
Avoid hardcoded paths.
Use configuration files instead.

6 Performance Expectations
Processing target:
100 videos < 1 minute
1000 videos < 5 minutes
Support parallel processing when possible.

7 Future Extensions
Planned features:
directory watcher
video embedding search
duplicate detection
quality filtering
automatic video editing
New features must be implemented as independent modules.
